Master Control is an independent administration app for a Telegram-based media
library. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Telegram, and it
does not use Telegram branding or artwork. The app icon and name are original.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored third-party source
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

TDLib (Telegram Database Library)
  Location in this repository : third_party/tdlib
  Version                     : 1.8.67 (pinned; see scripts/build-tdlib.sh)
  Upstream                    : https://github.com/tdlib/td
  License                     : Boost Software License 1.0
  License text                : third_party/tdlib/LICENSE_1_0.txt
  Copyright                   : Copyright (c) Telegram Inc. and TDLib authors

  TDLib is the Telegram engine Master Control talks to. It is distributed as
  source and compiled by scripts/build-tdlib.sh into libtdjson.so; no prebuilt
  TDLib binary is checked in. Only the JSON interface (tdjson) is used, reached
  through a single JNI bridge (telegram/src/main/java/.../TdJsonJni.kt).

OpenSSL
  Version                     : OpenSSL_1_1_1w (built by TDLib's own script)
  Upstream                    : https://www.openssl.org
  License                     : Apache License 2.0 (OpenSSL 1.1.1 and later)
  Note                        : Built at TDLib build time, not vendored in git.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Binary dependencies
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

All Kotlin/Android libraries are declared with pinned versions in
gradle/libs.versions.toml. Their licenses, upstream URLs and the reason each one
is used are listed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

Master Control re-implements no part of the MTProto protocol and contains no
hand-written Telegram cryptography; all Telegram protocol work is performed by
TDLib.
